WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.940
Panda gets Enthusiastic.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.890
What's wrong, Panda?

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.850
You seem a little down.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.590
Well, you see,

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.920
Mr. Full-time Panda is 
going back home to China

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:57.690
for a little while so he can 
attend a relative's wedding.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.780
Why would you be down because of that?

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.220
Well, you see...

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:08.710
Off

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:08.710
Off

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:08.710
Vacation

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:09.190
Full-time Panda Work Schedule

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.550
Since he's taking a full week off,

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:08.630
I have to work full-time 
for him that week.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:12.000
Your job at the zoo?

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.350
Yeah.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.650
But it's only for a week, right?

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.890
It's for a <i>whole</i> week.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:23.120
I wonder if I can get up early, 
not to mention everyday.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.830
I have no faith that I 
can actually do it.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.430
I think you have to worry more 
about the packed trains

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.830
rather than having to wake up early.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:34.170
Packed trains?

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.200
Packed trains are when 
the trains become

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.220
full with all the people 
heading to work.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:45.080
Us emperor penguins are used to it.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.210
What? You ride the trains, 
too, Mr. Penguin?

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.520
No.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.710
At the South Pole, all of us huddle

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.230
together and take care of the kids.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.150
It's really tight, 
like a packed train.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.730
It's like playing 
push and shove nonstop.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.570
Push and shove?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.290
That looks really fun.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.230
I'm actually starting 
to get really excited.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:19.130
I need to hurry home 
and get ready for tomorrow.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.000
Well then, thanks for the food!

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:28.000
I hope he'll be okay.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.980
I need to hurry!

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.920
Panda

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.940
If I don't hurry, I won't be able 
to ride the packed train!

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.390
Good morning, Panda.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.670
Good morning.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.270
Are you headed to work?

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.620
Good luck!

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.130
Off I go!

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.940
Excuse me.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.180
Hello.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.270
Could you pick out some flowers for me?

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:02.970
South Entrance

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.870
Wow, it really is like oshikura manju.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.320
The doors are closing.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.450
Please be careful.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.000
The doors are closing.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:28.260
Excuse me, where's the panda-only car?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.700
I don't think there is one.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.270
I-Is there anywhere that's open?

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.330
It's a little tight...

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.390
There will be a little shaking ahead,
 so please be careful.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.740
Hey, Panda!

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.160
It's time for your lunch.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.190
Could you just put it over there?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.080
I know it's tough to have to start work

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.710
so early in the morning,

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.400
but could you try to give the 
customers a little more service?

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.810
I don't want to ride in 
packed trains anymore.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:24.170
Could you work for me in the 
morning instead, Mr. Handa?

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.130
You can't really complain...

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:30.940
I'm going to come in a little later,

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:33.100
so could you be the 
panda in the morning?

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:36.310
I don't think that's going to work...

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:39.610
You'll be fine, you're shaped 
fairly close to a panda.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.520
No, no, no, no...

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.090
It's not happening!

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:55.470
Try to work a little harder! 
You promised!

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.360
I'm setting your lunch right here.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:58.990
Man...

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:08.780
I'm losing my appetite thinking 
about the packed trains.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:12.990
Panda.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.680
I have a delivery for you, Panda.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:22.820
Flowers?

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:28.570
"I'm always watching you.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:30.780
Please keep up your best at work.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.270
From your fan,

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:34.160
Rin Rin."

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:36.900
My fan?!

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.480
Rin Rin.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.660
I'm going to do my best!

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:49.240
Mom, Mr. Panda stood up!

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.930
That's amazing!

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:53.370
Panda

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.820
Rin Rin.

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:03.980
I'm heading off!

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.610
Could it be?

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.370
Rin Rin?

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.990
Hello?

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:20.350
Panda

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.150
Rin Rin?

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:39.670
I'll do my best, okay?

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:41.920
Panda

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.890
Rin Rin will be watching me.

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:20.640
<i>Rin Rin must be somewhere 
in that crowd.</i>

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:24.810
Panda's working really hard lately.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.520
But I wonder why.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:31.280
Thanks for all your good work.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:35.370
Mr. Full-time Panda came 
back today, right?

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:45.960
Sweet Roasted 
Chestnut Chocolates{Z: if this is chocolates perhaps something more like "Chocolate-covered Roasted Chestnuts" would be better?}

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.100
He brought gifts.

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:44.390
I heard you weren't late 
once this week, Panda.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:45.960
That's really impressive.

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:50.960
Someone really dear to me 
has been watching me.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:56.140
But it looks like you're really tired.

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:00.030
You look really beat up and 
dirty in various places.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.880
You may actually be working too hard.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:04.390
I think you should take a break.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:08.760
I can't let her see me 
looking like this.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:09.750
"Her"?

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.910
I'm gonna head home.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:16.330
Hey! You're forgetting your 
Sweet Roasted Chestnut chocolates.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:18.320
Panda

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:34.570
"You were great yesterday.

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:36.760
Please do your best today, too!"

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.490
I worked really hard 
this week, Rin Rin.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:56.650
Panda

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.890
I have to hurry!

00:09:55.890 --> 00:10:01.470
I wonder if Rin Rin thinks I'll 
be there early today, too.

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:04.120
It'd be awful if we just 
missed each other.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.590
Good morning, Panda.

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:11.630
Good morning!

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.760
Aren't you going back 
to part-time today?

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:18.510
Huh? Uh, yes.

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:20.600
That's what I thought.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:21.930
I got scared for a moment.

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:25.660
Did you like the flowers 
I picked out for you?

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:29.570
Oh, the flowers Rin Rin got for me?

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:31.360
I'm taking good care of them.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:33.180
Oh, that's right!

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.900
I have something I want to show you.

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:36.400
Wait here.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:39.080
Look.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.950
Rin Rin's not here today?

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.180
Oh, I'm Rin Rin.

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:54.750
H
a
y
a
s
h
i 

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.400
My name is Hayashi Rintarou.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:54.730
R
i
n 

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:57.720
I love pandas!

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:01.520
Oh, and you're one of the best, Panda!

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:18.360
Rin Rin's best photo is this.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:23.560
It's my favorite, so I had it blown up.

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.020
I'll give you a copy, too.

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:38.750
I don't want it.

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:43.790
I'm giving these back.

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:44.430
But why?!

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:46.900
Hey, Panda!

00:11:48.970 --> 00:12:02.950
Polar  
Bear's 
Café

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:07.910
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:07.040
Everyone's Parfait

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.020
Hello.

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:16.550
Polar Bear?

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:21.400
What's wrong?

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.250
Is something on your mind?

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:25.840
This.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:27.760
Candies?

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.790
I was trying to figure out

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:32.600
why traffic lights are 
these three colors.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:34.760
I see.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:36.490
That's not it, Panda.

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:40.550
Mr. Polar Bear is trying to figure 
out a special menu for the café.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.450
A special menu?

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:49.920
I failed the skills test again.

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:51.190
Skills test?

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.290
Oh, at the driving school.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.770
That instructor is too picky, anyway!

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:58.250
How were they picky?

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.350
Like he was telling me,

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:02.190
"Stop looking all over the place 
and watch where you're going,"

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:04.190
or "Stop panicking,"

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:05.380
or "Stop flapping around so much

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.510
when you're holding the wheel."

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:10.720
I think he has a point.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.780
At this rate, I'll never be able to

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:15.100
ask Miss Penko out on a driving date,

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.650
because of that instructor.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:18.650
Date <i>(de-to)</i>?

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.890
That would be a tent <i>(tento)</i>.

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:25.150
That's a boxed lunch <i>(bento)</i>.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.200
That would be an electric light <i>(dento)</i>.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.830
Certain
Victory

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.830
Heart

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.830
Captain

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.830
That would be kendo.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:32.830
I said "date!"

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.790
I wonder how I can make her mine?

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:40.850
Make her yours?

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:44.170
What would you do, Polar Bear?

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:47.030
I'd wait.

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:49.090
You'd wait?

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:51.490
I would earnestly wait.

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:53.980
Wow, you're such an adult.

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:57.320
Yes, if you can't do that, 
you can't become an adult.

00:13:57.320 --> 00:13:58.580
You can't?

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:02.390
Earnestly wait,

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:03.740
and wait,

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:04.850
and wait,

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:09.470
until they finally come out!

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:13.540
That's not making them yours <i>(itomeru)</i>!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.200
That's taking them down <i>(shitomeru)</i>!

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:18.240
Would you think about this 
seriously, Polar Bear?!

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:23.630
I just had an idea, 
looking at you, Mr. Penguin.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:25.590
Huh? What?

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:29.000
How about a parfait fair, Miss Sasako?

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.530
Parfaits? That's a great idea.

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:33.300
What the heck?

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:35.560
That has nothing to do with dates.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.860
How in the world did you 
get to that subject?

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:41.260
We were just talking about 
making a special menu,

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:43.020
but we couldn't figure 
out what it should be.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.840
So your special menu is 
going to have parfaits?

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:48.990
I love parfaits!

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.760
Parfaits are a great idea,

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:55.390
but isn't "parfait fair" 
a bit hard to say?

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.790
No, it'll be fine.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:58.960
All right, it's settled.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.390
We'll call it "parhay hair."

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:06.110
You couldn't say it.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:13.850
Polar  
Bear's 
Café

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.770
In Preparations

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:26.380
Strawberry parfait, banana 
parfait, chocolate parfait.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.690
These are definitely parfaits,

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:32.530
but it'd be boring to have just 
the normal lineup for the fair.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:38.120
Hmm, special parfaits, huh?

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:40.600
Books

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:48.360
Cooking

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.490
Mr. Polar Bear.

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:53.640
Parfait Fair.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:54.890
Huh?

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.000
You're having one, right?

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.030
Have you decided on the menu yet?

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:00.560
I'm trying to decide as we speak.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:04.270
Then how about a mandrill parfait?

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:06.270
What's that?

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:08.770
It is a parfait that is a mandrill.

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:12.240
And it is... <i>intense</i>!

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:16.060
I don't think parfaits need intensity.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.560
Hmm, special parfaits, huh?

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:23.640
Well, if it isn't Mr. Polar Bear.

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:25.460
Oh, hello, Mr. Llama.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:26.710
Hello.

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:28.840
So, I heard the news.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:29.860
What?

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.060
You're going to have a 
parfait fair, right?

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:35.610
I thought up a spectacular parfait.

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:38.600
It's a parfait, but it's very healthy.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:41.310
Sounds great. What is it?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.100
One of my best ideas.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:45.560
A parfait with a large 
serving of grass.

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:49.530
To explain the parfait 
in further detail,

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:53.320
there's grass on top of the plate...

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.280
A plate?

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:57.840
And on top of that, 
there'll be boiled grass...

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.350
and then freshly delivered 
grass from the fields...

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:05.010
will hang over the dish.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:09.340
Well, that's definitely not a parfait.

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:11.720
If you had to call it something, 
it'd probably be a salad.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:16.220
Hmm, special parfaits...

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:21.420
Mr. Polar Bear...

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:23.740
Over here...

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:28.190
Please wait...

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:35.110
I have... something to tell you.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:42.200
What's the matter, Mr. Tortoise?

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:45.470
Parfai... fai...

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:46.980
Parfait fair?

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:51.750
How about a shell parfait?

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:54.300
Shell parfait?

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:03.190
That might be a little hard to eat.

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:07.600
Hmm, special parfaits...

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:11.320
I wonder what would be good.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:15.680
Mr. Polar Bear!

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.720
Oh, hello, Anteater.

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:19.200
I thought of...

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:22.450
I thought of a great parfait!

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:25.870
What kind of parfait is it?

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.640
The topping is absolutely amazing!

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:31.090
Visually, it looks like black sesame,

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:34.090
but they're wriggling!

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:38.300
No, I'm going to pass.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:42.680
But they're like lively 
black sesame that wriggle!

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:49.870
Japanese style is good, too, but...

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:51.900
What's wrong, Polar Bear?

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:54.390
I need to hurry up and decide on

00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:56.050
the menu for the parfait fair.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:58.120
Everyone's going crazy.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:18:59.410
Going crazy?

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:01.630
Since it's the special menu,

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:04.270
I'm guessing everyone is 
looking forward to it.

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:06.230
Hey!

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:07.870
I have a great idea!

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:10.310
Here you go!

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:13.070
This is it! The bamboo parfait!

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:15.510
I got Panda's advice 
and tried to make it.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:17.050
Isn't it amazing?

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:20.070
You start with bamboo jello and 
bamboo grass whipped cream,

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:23.640
then top it with fresh bamboo 
grass and bamboo shoots,

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.660
and finish it off with 
lots of bamboo shavings!

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.600
That's a very green parfait.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.880
I don't think anyone would eat 
it other than you, Panda.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:37.250
Really? Even though it 
looks this delicious?

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.120
The bamboo shavings look like 
they'll stab you in the mouth.

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:44.420
You probably think that anything 
can be on a parfait, Panda.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.990
We can't leave it up to you.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:49.460
Here, I'll throw in my idea, too.

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:51.960
A sardine parfait.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:56.250
It's full of DHA and it'll 
make you smart.

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:58.640
No?

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:01.930
Well, horse mackerel 
are in season, too.

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:03.890
Let's avoid fish altogether.

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:07.860
I wouldn't call that a parfait...

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:09.550
It's more like fancy sashimi.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:13.170
Oh, how about this?

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:20.570
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.030
How about a panda parfait?

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:27.950
The panda's head is made 
with vanilla ice cream,

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:29.900
and its face and ears are 
made with chocolate.

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:36.100
Wow, pandas are cute even as parfaits!

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:39.600
Then there's the bear bear parfait.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:42.260
I made it with vanilla 
and coffee ice cream.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.430
That's good!

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:46.130
The south pole parfait.

00:20:46.130 --> 00:20:48.830
I made a glacier with shaved ice.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:49.910
Wow!

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:52.380
How cute! Are these new?

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:54.950
Oh no, they're test products.

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:56.510
You're welcome to try 
them if you'd like.

00:20:56.510 --> 00:20:58.020
Wow, really?

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.860
Well then, thanks for the food!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.740
Let's start with the panda.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:09.120
And then the penguin.

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:13.790
And then the polar bear.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:20.120
I think I'll eat the nose, too.

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:23.470
Oh, how mean! I'll have some, too.

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:27.110
Please put these on your menu!

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:30.610
How wonderful! They're a hit.

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:34.940
Y-Yeah, great...

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:43.940
Polar  
Bear's 
Café

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.880
Hey, listen to this!

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:51.300
I failed the test again!

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:02.250
This place is a lot 
busier than usual.

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:03.620
What happened?

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:06.680
Apparently the new menu 
items are a hit.

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:09.010
Oh, the parfait fair?

00:22:11.960 --> 00:22:14.180
The one plate lunch fair.

00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:24.840
Special Menu

00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:24.840
One Plate Lunch

00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:24.840
We are sold out.

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:23.610
So it wasn't parfaits...

00:23:54.930 --> 00:24:24.520
Next Time

00:23:59.030 --> 00:24:01.130
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:01.130 --> 00:24:03.000
What's wrong, Panda?

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:04.590
Without asking me the details,

00:24:04.590 --> 00:24:07.000
could I have your bank book?

00:24:07.360 --> 00:24:09.670
How about no?

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:11.960
Wrap it up, Polar Bear.

00:24:11.960 --> 00:24:14.100
Next time, Polar Bear's Café...

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:18.180
will be presented in Portuguese.

00:24:18.180 --> 00:24:19.450
Let's go with Japanese.

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:24.520
Panda's Diet
Strive for it! Wild Panda

00:24:19.450 --> 00:24:20.390
Enjoy!
